## 1. Locators

**Standard:** Role/label first (`getByRole` → `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` → `getByText` → `getByTestId` escape hatch); never CSS/XPath; locators in POM constructors; disambiguate with `.filter({ hasText })`, not `.first()`.

✅ **Good** (from `pages/ProgramsPage.ts`):

```typescript
this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' });
this.programRow = (name: string) =>
  page.getByRole('row').filter({ has: page.getByText(name, { exact: true }) });
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
page.locator('.programs-table tr:nth-child(2)');          // CSS + positional
await programsPage.programRow(name).first().click();     // .first() masks ambiguity
```

**Why:** CSS/XPath and `.first()` bind to DOM structure, not user-visible labels — tests pass on the wrong row or break after unrelated UI refactors.

---

## 2. Waiting

**Standard:** Web-first assertions only (`expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `.toBeEnabled()` / `.toHaveText()`); never `waitForTimeout` or snapshot `await locator.isVisible()`.

✅ **Good** (from `tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.programNameField).toBeVisible();
await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.createButton).toBeEnabled();
```

❌ **Bad** (anti-pattern; still present in `pages/ProgramsPage.ts` — do not copy):

```typescript
await page.waitForTimeout(100);
expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

**Why:** Fixed delays race the app (too short → flake, too long → slow); snapshot booleans do not auto-retry when the DOM updates a moment later.

---

## 3. Page Objects

**Standard:** One POM per page/component in `pages/`; `readonly` locators in the constructor; action methods only — all `expect(...)` stay in specs.

✅ **Good** (from `tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
const programsPage = new ProgramsPage(page);
await programsPage.goto();
await programsPage.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.programNameField).toBeVisible();
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
await page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' }).click();  // inline locator in spec
// inside pages/ProgramsPage.ts:
expect(await this.heading.isVisible()).toBe(true);                  // assertion in POM
```

**Why:** Inline locators duplicate and drift from POMs; assertions in POMs hide intent and cannot use Playwright's test-scoped retry/reporting.

