## 4. Auth

**Standard:** Stored session by default via the `setup` project (`auth.setup.ts` → `playwright/.auth/user.json`); login-page tests only use empty `storageState` + UI login; API login for bulk setup or stale sessions (`auth-strategy.md`).

✅ **Good** (from `tests/auth-reuse.spec.ts` — relies on config `storageState`):

```typescript
test('reuse 1 — programs page loads authenticated', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto(`${BASE_URL}/programs`);
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Programs', level: 2 })).toBeVisible();
});
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(process.env.DIDAXIS_EMAIL!);
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign In' }).click();  // every test
});
```

**Why:** Per-test UI login adds seconds of flake surface and hides auth regressions that `storageState` reuse is meant to catch.

