## 7. Network mocking

**Standard:** Use `page.route` / `route.fulfill` for 500/503/timeout/empty/malformed (plus 401/403/404/3xx); read live error/empty copy before asserting; never mock the endpoint under test; tag `{ tag: '@regression' }` (UI + mock).

✅ **Good** (from `tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts` TC-011 — tighten URL in new tests):

```typescript
await page.route('**/api/programs**', async (route) => {
  if (route.request().method() === 'POST') {
    await route.fulfill({ status: 503, contentType: 'application/json', body: '{}' });
    return;
  }
  await route.continue();
});
await programsPage.newProgramModal.clickCreate();
await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();  // modal stays open
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
await page.route('**/*', async (route) => route.abort());  // blocks auth, assets, unrelated APIs
await expect(page.getByText('Something went wrong')).toBeVisible();  // invented copy
```

**Why:** Broad routes intercept traffic the test still needs; invented strings pass while the UI shows nothing or different copy (`ds4` TC-013 notes delete errors may be silent).

