## 9. Assertions

**Standard:** Web-first hard `expect` for AC gates; `expect.soft` for independent multi-check audits; `toHaveScreenshot` only when visual regression is the AC (human-approved baseline, `{ tag: '@visual' }`).

✅ **Good** (from `tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
await expect(programsPage.programRow(programName)).toHaveCount(1);
await expect(programsPage.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeHidden({ timeout: 15000 });
```

✅ **Soft audit** *(advised — see `playwright-assertions` skill)*:

```typescript
await expect.soft(programsPage.programNameInRow(name)).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(programsPage.programDescriptionInRow(name)).toBeVisible();
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
expect(await programsPage.programRow(name).count()).toBe(1);  // no auto-retry
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot();                         // visual without baseline/AC
await expect.soft(criticalSubmitButton).toBeEnabled();         // soft on must-pass gate
```

**Why:** Non-retrying reads flake on slow renders; unapproved screenshots pass on any first pixel dump; soft asserts on critical gates hide the failure that blocks the user.

